# Renders to a file from the window (scripts\verify\panel.ps1, part render), live:
#   RayTracingViewer cornell -w 320 --height 180 -s 16 --input tests\window-render.input
# Each render's files must be the bytes of the RayTracingGPU command it printed, run; the window's own view must come
# back at its own size after each; a render cancelled must save nothing.
#
# The Cornell box (CUDA) at 96x54 and 64 samples: cornell-render-001.png and .pfm
at 0 action render 96 54 64
# still-life (OptiX) at 96x54, 16 samples asked for, rendered as a whole round of 64, with its denoised copy:
# still-life-render-002.png, .pfm and -denoised.png (the files of a run are numbered in turn, whatever the scene)
at 60 action scene still-life
at 90 action render 96 54 16 denoised
# Back to the Cornell box: a render far too long, cancelled after a few frames
at 150 action scene cornell
at 170 action render 1920 1080 1000000
at 176 action render-cancel
# The window's own view, saved as P saves it: 320x180 again
at 200 action save
at 220 quit
